<title>CHINA: Hong Kong tycoon gives $1 mln to Shanghai college.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong tycoon gives $1 mln to Shanghai college.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daniel Koo, president of Shui Hing Co, has contributed $1 million to Shanda College, Shanghai's first private college since 1949, to pay for its main campus building, the Business News said on Monday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the building, in the Jinqiao area of the Pudong development zone to the east of Shanghai's city centre, has a total floor area of 4,677 square metres, and holds up to 1,500 students. It is already in use.</p>
